  "final_span": "on a fourth-and-2 from the Rockets\u2019 5.\n\"We ran it twice up the middle and got no movement so I knew there was a little spice and a little something-something in there,\" Harbison said. \"We just played with each other.\n\"I didn\u2019t want anything; I wanted us to be successful overall. And the play was pretty much Tre\u2019s, honestly.\n\"It made up for a lot of the mistakes I\u2019ve made on the season.\"\nAfter a defensive holding penalty, Childers substituted for starter Daniel Santacaterina, pushing the Huskies back. Toledo reimbursed Childers, since Lance Carlson intercepted a tipped pass on NIU's opening drive, positioning himself at the right flat.\nNIU had chances to defeat Toledo in the last seven minutes of the first half, but missed converting them.\nAs the Huskies were down 9-7 and had the ball on Toledo's 15, Santacaterina received the snap for a shot-gun sweep right on second downs. He accumulated only 3 yards, causing the drive to stall and result in his dropout.\nOn fourth down and 7, Santacaterina took his stance and threw a long pass towards the Bison 8. Jermaine Marshall of Toledo inflicted a blow to Santacaterina's head via a helmet-to-helmet hit, causing the Huskies to fail in their attempt to score an extra point for a tie.\n\"It\u2019s a part of the game, next play,\" Santacaterina said. \"I\u2019ve learned from it. We were at halftime, tied, so next play.\"\nHe completed 10 worry-passes in just over an eighth of a game, with five going to tight end Lance Lenoir for 58 yards, but the Pack received two penalties on the drive.\nAfter the second half started, failing to get the extra point kept the score tied. NIU seemed poised to use up the remaining time when fullback Rani Ilino, who had not been a factor all season leading up to Wednesday, sprinted for a 9-yard scoring run. Childers and Harbison converted a fourth-and-1 on the two",
